/F2 9 Tf (## 3. Acoustic Survey Deck-Machinery Lockout & $A'$ Window Separation) Tj /F1 8 Tf T*
(1. **Acoustic Survey Lockout \(`G3` `forbids_deck_machinery_while_active=True`\)**:) Tj T*
(   - Regardless of whether **14** or **6** crew are aboard, while **G3** is in `SURVEY_QUIET` \(`1 kW`,) Tj T*
( `2-6 kn`\), hydraulic A-frames, winches \(`G2`\), and flight-deck handling gear \(`G4`\) are **locked ) Tj T*
(out** to prevent acoustic corruption of the seabed survey sonar.) Tj T*
(   - To launch or recover **G4** \(`UAV_SAR`\) or deploy **G2** \(`ROV_INSPECTION`\), the governor must ) Tj T*
(first issue `ACOUSTIC_HOLD` to **G3**, wait for the mandatory **`15 s` acoustic modem handshake** ) Tj T*
(\(`10-60 s` spec\), and confirm G3 is in `HOLD_ACOUSTIC` before unlocking deck machinery or turning into) Tj T*
( the wind.) Tj T*
(2. **Separation of Normal Flight Window vs. $A'$ At-Sea Replacement Window \(`CRW-03`\)**:) Tj T*
(   - **Normal G4 Flight Launch/Recovery**: vessel speed **`5-12 kn`**, wind **$\\le 25\\text{ kn}$**, ) Tj T*
(Sea State **$\\le 4$**, heading aligned within $\\pm 15^\\circ$ of wind, **`2` deck crew**.) Tj T*
(   - **$A'$ At-Sea Vehicle Replacement**: vessel speed **`4-8 kn`**, wind **$\\le 20\\text{ kn}$**, Sea ) Tj T*
(State **$\\le 3$** \(`G4`, `3` crew / `30 min`\) or **$\\le 4$** \(`G3`, `4` crew / `45 min`\). At `10 kn` ) Tj T*
(and `22 kn` wind, normal UAV recovery is admitted \(`YES`\), whereas at-sea vehicle replacement is ) Tj T*
(rejected \(`NOT_NOW` / blocked by $A'$ envelope\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
() Tj T*
/F2 9 Tf (## 4. Fault Governance Under Reduced and Uncrewed Regimes \(`RUN-03`, `RUN-04`, `SAF-01`\)) Tj /F1 8 Tf T*
(When operating with **6** or **0** crew, physical manual intervention on tripped breakers or ) Tj T*
(overheated racks is slow \(**6 crew**\) or impossible \(**0 crew**\). The governor enforces three ) Tj T*
(automated fail-safe barriers:) Tj T*
(- **Urgent Safety Commands \(`STOP`, `HOLD`, `SECURE` $\\le 200\\text{ ms}$, `SAF-01`\)**: Routed strictly) Tj T*
( over the dual `10 Gbps` local shipboard LAN \(`<5 ms` transport latency\), never over `600-800 ms` ) Tj T*
(SATCOM. Measured execution latency on both MacBook Pro and the `aarch64` Linux board \(`training06`\) is) Tj T*
( **`< 1 ms`** \($\\ll 200\\text{ ms}$ budget\).) Tj T*
(- **Guest Overconsumption \(`+10%` to `+20%`, `RUN-04`\)**: Because none of `G1`-`G5` is safety-critical) Tj T*
( by design, if a payload \(e.g., `G5` declared `45 kW` drawing `54 kW` = `+20%`\) exceeds its manifest ) Tj T*
(envelope, 1:1 thermal coupling immediately adds `+9 kW` to the chilled-water ledger and the governor ) Tj T*
(autonomously throttles `G5` to `DEGRADED_70PCT_LOSS` \(`8 kW`\) while protecting active ) Tj T*
(uninterruptible/recovery tasks \(`G3` recharge, `G4` flight/recovery\).) Tj T*
(- **Lost or Stale Telemetry Feeds \(`RUN-03`\)**: If `seawater_temp_c` exceeds its `5,000 ms` TTL ) Tj T*
(\(`STALE` / `UNAVAILABLE`\), the governor never extrapolates optimistic cooling; it clamps to the ) Tj T*
(conservative **$30\\,^\\circ\\text{C}$ \(`120 kW` nominal / `72 kW` degraded\)** thermal bound until sensor) Tj T*
( freshness is restored.) Tj T*
